From 39d279da65fb4dccbd482994920388c06a756479 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: k114s-integration <integration@localhost>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:46:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] kboot: T6050: hand the K114s camera over on 27.2

The camera hand-off row is keyed by board compatible, sensor type and firmware. aura #188
added the K116s (0xbc on 27.2) and #206 the K114c. The 14-inch M5 Pro OLED (K114s, Mac17,13,
"apple,k114s") has no row, so dt_set_t6050_isp() returns -1 ("board or firmware not in the
table") and the ISP stays disabled.

Add {"apple,k114s", 0xba, V27_2}. The value is read from a K114s ADT on macOS 27.2 (26B8125):
isp0 sensor-type 0xba, firmware uuid 980F533B-34EA-3FBA-878C-809F6AF57345 (the K116s one),
cam-connections-scheme 0x10, and two segment-ranges of 0xc1c000 and 0x13d0000 bytes at iova 0 and
0xc1c000, remap 0x10000000000 and 0x10000c1c000: every check that follows the table passes on
that ADT (replayed in tests/k114s-adt-camera-facts.py of chrisohearn/omarchy-m5p-oled).

Nothing else is loosened. K114s on 27.3 stays refused, as the K116s does. Not booted: no K114s
has run this hand-off, and the kernel needs a K114s tree that includes t6050-j716c-isp.dtsi.

K114s integration (chrisohearn/omarchy-m5p-oled).
---
 src/kboot.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kboot.c b/src/kboot.c
index f5da83b..ddf4f7b 100644
--- a/src/kboot.c
+++ b/src/kboot.c
@@ -9378,8 +9378,8 @@ t6050_isp_segments_valid(const struct adt_segment_ranges *seg, u32 len, u64 ram,
  * T6050 firmware lives below Linux RAM. Publish current ADT ranges, not
  * snapshot physical addresses. The kernel allocates the small main-memory
  * tail and owns all power, DART and firmware-start operations. J716c (0x75)
- * and J714s (0x74) on 27.0, K114c (0xb9) on 27.3 beta and K116s (0xbc) on
- * 27.2 use the same two segment names.
+ * and J714s (0x74) on 27.0, K114c (0xb9) on 27.3 beta and K116s (0xbc) and
+ * K114s (0xba) on 27.2 use the same two segment names.
  */
 __attribute__((section(".init.t6050_isp"))) static int t6050_isp_add_mem_region(uint32_t phandle,
                                                                                 const char *name)
@@ -9406,6 +9406,12 @@ static const struct {
      * the IPSW's isp_bni/adc-nyx-sck11pm; its K116 connection table has one FrontRGB IMX958.
      */
     {"apple,k116s", 0xbc, V27_2},
+    /*
+     * K114s (14-inch M5 Pro OLED, Mac17,13): ADT isp0 of 27.2 (26B8125). The same firmware uuid,
+     * connection scheme 0x10, interrupts, DARTs and two segments as the K116s; only the sensor
+     * type differs (0xba). Read from a K114s ADT; no K114s has booted this hand-off yet.
+     */
+    {"apple,k114s", 0xba, V27_2},
 };
 
 static int dt_set_t6050_isp(const char **why)
-- 
